# Component Rules

## Existing Patterns — Use These
- Reveal — scroll-driven fade/slide reveal: src/components/ui/reveal.tsx
- StaggerReveal + staggerChild — staggered children reveal
- LenisProvider — smooth scroll wrapper (already in layout, never add another)

## Animation Standards
- All whileInView must use viewport={{ once: true }}
- Only animate transform and opacity — never width, height, top, left
- GPU-accelerated properties only — no layout-triggering animations
- Lenis is globally configured — never add a second scroll instance
- Use useSpring for weighted, cinematic scroll feels
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion always

## Framer Motion Patterns
- useScroll + useTransform for scroll-linked values
- useInView for time-based stagger animations
- staggerChildren: 0.12-0.15, delayChildren: 0.3-0.4 for cascades
- Duration 0.8-1.0s for premium feel — never fast bouncy animations
- Ease [0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1] for cinematic motion

## Accessibility
- All images need alt text
- All form inputs need labels
- Ensure keyboard navigability for all interactive elements
- Implement ARIA labels and roles on interactive components
- Color contrast minimum 4.5:1 (WCAG 2.1 AA)
- Use semantic HTML elements

## Icons
- Use Lucide React only — never emojis as icons
- Always include aria-label on icon-only buttons

## Component Quality
- Minimal props — break complex components into smaller parts
- Use composition over large monolithic components
- Export reusable subcomponents when they might be used elsewhere